//  direct-MLIR negatives: the structured #neutrino.expr var leaves are
// SSA-slot-bound (amendments 1 & 2), and the op verifier proves the slot <->
// dependency bijection — a var cannot reference a value absent from the op's
// declared deps (compute deps / an entry's guard_deps), and no declared dep is
// dead. The valid IR round-trips through the custom AttrDef printer/parser.
//
// RUN: %neutrino-translate %S/coordination_plan.neu > %t.mlir
//
// Valid structured IR verifies and round-trips (print/parse the recursive attr):
// RUN: %neutrino-opt %t.mlir | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VALID
// VALID: #neutrino.expr<cmp extension 0 -1 ">="
//
// A COMPUTE var leaf bound to a non-existent dependency slot is rejected — the
// var references a value not among the op's SSA deps:
// RUN: sed 's/<var money 0 0/<var money 0 9/' %t.mlir > %t.badcompute.mlir
// RUN: %not %neutrino-opt %t.badcompute.mlir 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADSLOT
// BADSLOT: [expr.slot]{{.*}}references dep slot 9
//
// A GUARD var leaf with no matching guard dependency is rejected the same way
// (its slot is outside the entry's guard_deps segment):
// RUN: sed 's/<var money 0 1/<var money 0 7/' %t.mlir > %t.badguard.mlir
// RUN: %not %neutrino-opt %t.badguard.mlir 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADGUARD
// BADGUARD: [expr.slot]{{.*}}dep slot 7
//
// A CARRIED dtype that disagrees with the inferred category is rejected (
// P1) — a `money` var laundered as `string` cannot pass a "typed, verified" IR
// (structure + deps stay valid; only the dtype lies):
// RUN: sed 's/<var money 0 0/<var string 0 0/' %t.mlir > %t.baddtype.mlir
// RUN: %not %neutrino-opt %t.baddtype.mlir 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADDTYPE
// BADDTYPE: [expr.type]{{.*}}carries dtype 'string' but its inferred category is 'money'
//
// The provenance TEXT must parse to the SAME structure as the AST ( P1) —
// tampering the `when` text while leaving the guard ast intact is rejected:
// RUN: sed 's/amount >= threshold/amount > threshold/' %t.mlir > %t.badprov.mlir
// RUN: %not %neutrino-opt %t.badprov.mlir 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADPROV
// BADPROV: [expr.provenance]{{.*}}does not match the structured ast
//
// DUPLICATE dependency operands are rejected ( P2): passing the same value
// in two guard-dep slots would make canonical identity operand-layout-dependent.
// RUN: sed 's/, %3, %4)/, %3, %3)/' %t.mlir > %t.dupdep.mlir
// RUN: %not %neutrino-opt %t.dupdep.mlir 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DUPDEP
// DUPDEP: [expr.slot]{{.*}}more than once
